// =============================================================================
// Warden Alric — Resource Steward / Upgrade Hall (THE MASTER QUEST).
// Questline: "Rebuild Elarion" (vendor.steward).  Keystone-SINK, not source:
// his stages GATE on the keystones the other vendors granted (HasKeystone /
// KeystoneCount — NPCCommandBridge). Final stage awakens the Spire.
// =============================================================================
title: TalkToSteward
---
<<if $q_steward_stage == 0>>
    Alric: Elarion was a fortress once. We can be again — but a wall is only as strong as the hands that built it. Bring me the realm's crafts, and I'll bring back the light.
    -> I'll rebuild Elarion with you.
        Alric: Then it begins. First, raise the village itself — we need the Granary and the Lumbermill restored before a single new wall goes up.
        <<set $q_steward_stage = 1>>
        <<StartQuest vendor.steward>>
        Alric: Mother Wren and Old Pell first. Come back with their Keystones.
    -> Open the Upgrade Hall.
        <<OpenUpgrade "steward">>
<<elseif $q_steward_stage == 1>>
    <<if HasKeystone("FullGranary") and HasKeystone("HeartwoodSapling")>>
        Alric: The Granary brims and the forest greens. The village can rise to Tier 2.
        -> Raise the village.
            <<AdvanceQuest vendor.steward>>
            <<set $q_steward_stage = 2>>
            Alric: Elarion stands taller already. Now — re-arm the walls. That needs the Forge and the Armorer: Borin's Emberbrand and Halvard's Oathshield.
    <<else>>
        Alric: Not yet. I need the Full Granary from Mother Wren and the Heartwood Sapling from Old Pell before the village can grow. Restore the food and the forests first.
        -> Open the Upgrade Hall.
            <<OpenUpgrade "steward">>
    <<endif>>
<<elseif $q_steward_stage == 2>>
    <<if HasKeystone("Emberbrand") and HasKeystone("Oathshield")>>
        Alric: A lit forge and tested plate. The walls can bare their teeth again.
        -> Re-arm the walls.
            <<AdvanceQuest vendor.steward>>
            <<set $q_steward_stage = 3>>
            Alric: The ramparts answer now. Last before the end — rekindle the wards. Bring me Sable's First Heartgem and Fenn's Bonded Beast.
    <<else>>
        Alric: The walls are still bare. I need the Emberbrand from Borin and the Oathshield from Halvard. Light the forge, plate the line.
        -> Open the Upgrade Hall.
            <<OpenUpgrade "steward">>
    <<endif>>
<<elseif $q_steward_stage == 3>>
    <<if HasKeystone("FirstHeartgem") and HasKeystone("BondedBeast")>>
        Alric: Heartgem and Bonded Beast both. The wards will hold.
        -> Rekindle the wards.
            <<AdvanceQuest vendor.steward>>
            Alric: <i>Light kindles along the ramparts.</i> It is enough. With the realm's crafts gathered, the Spire can rise.
            <<jump StewardFinale>>
    <<else>>
        Alric: The wards lie cold. I need the First Heartgem from Sable and the Bonded Beast from Fenn before they'll catch.
        -> Open the Upgrade Hall.
            <<OpenUpgrade "steward">>
    <<endif>>
<<else>>
    Alric: The Spire stands and the Heart burns bright, thanks to you. Elarion is whole. But keep your edge — the realm always needs its Warden's hand.
    -> Open the Upgrade Hall.
        <<OpenUpgrade "steward">>
    -> Nothing today.
        Alric: The light holds. Go in strength.
<<endif>>
===

// ── Finale gate: needs the convergence count (>=6 of 8 vendor Keystones). ──
title: StewardFinale
---
<<if KeystoneCount() >= 6>>
    Alric: Six Keystones and more — the realm's crafts are restored. The Spire answers!
    -> Awaken the Spire.
        <<AdvanceQuest vendor.steward>>
        <<GiveKeystone "SpireAwakened">>
        <<set $q_steward_stage = 9>>
        Alric: <i>The Spire rises from the Heart, blazing.</i> Now we hold it — survive the Spire's defense, then we march on the Orc Necromancer in the Ashen Wastes. Win, and the Heart of Elarion is relit. Stand with me, Defender. This is the last call.
<<else>>
    Alric: The wards are kindled, but the Spire needs more of the realm behind it — six Keystones at least, and you carry {KeystoneCount()}. Finish the vendors' threads, then return to me.
    -> I'll gather the rest.
        Alric: Every craft restored is a stone in the Spire. Go.
<<endif>>
===
